//? Title: Gnome Sort: The Pointer Walk and Its Exact Cost
//? Subtitle: Native stable identities, actual loop records and inversion-controlled experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sort a sequence of integers while keeping equal values in their original order.
A short loop can do this by moving one pointer forwards over ordered pairs and
backwards after exchanging an inverted pair. This report follows actual native
execution on three values, repeats the original seven-value walk, and checks
stability through carried identities. A decreasing potential explains the exact
cost: n values with I strict inversions require n+2I loop visits. Controlled input
families, key-comparison counts and resource limits show what that identity does
and does not measure. Every table and figure is generated by complete C++ programs.
)

\toc

> Follow two actual exchanges

Start with [3,1,2] and pointer i=0. At the boundary, advance without comparing
keys. Otherwise compare a[i−1] and a[i]. If they are ordered, advance; if they are
strictly inverted, exchange them and step back. The native trace records that
executing loop, including the before-pair values and their original identities.
It does not run another sorting loop to reconstruct a history.

In the following diagram, key@id names a value and its zero-based original
position. Both exchanges involve key 3, first with key 1 and then with key 2.
The complete table also retains the boundary and ordered forward visits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gnome_pairs.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gnome_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const auto t=dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_trace({3,1,2});
 std::vector<dm::algorithms::GnomeSortEvent> swaps;
 std::print("| visit | pointer before | compared pair | swapped | pointer after |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | --- | ---: |\n");
 for(const auto& e:t.events)if(e.kind==dm::algorithms::GnomeSortEventKind::step){
  const auto pair=e.compared?std::format("{}@{} : {}@{}",e.left,e.left_original_index,e.right,e.right_original_index):"boundary; no comparison";
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",e.ordinal,e.index_before,pair,e.swapped,e.index_after);
  if(e.swapped)swaps.push_back(e);
 }
 std::print("\nOutput {}; original indices {}; visits {}; key comparisons {}; swaps {}; complete records {}.\n",t.run.output,t.run.original_indices,t.run.work.visits,t.run.work.key_comparisons,t.run.work.swaps,t.events.size());
 if(swaps.size()!=2)throw std::runtime_error("two actual exchanges");
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(68,1050);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.5;box.height=1.7;box.font_size=22;
 for(std::size_t j=0;j<swaps.size();++j){
  const auto& e=swaps[j];const double y=-3.1*double(j);
  const auto left=std::format("before{}",j),right=std::format("after{}",j);
  d.node(left,{0,y},std::format("Compared pair\n{}@{} : {}@{}\ni = {}",e.left,e.left_original_index,e.right,e.right_original_index,e.index_before),box)
   .node(right,{6.8,y},std::format("After actual exchange\n{}@{} : {}@{}\ni = {}",e.right,e.right_original_index,e.left,e.left_original_index,e.index_after),box)
   .edge(left,right,"swap");
 }
 d.text({3.4,2},"Two exchanges from the same native execution",24).save_svg("build/gnome_pairs.svg");
 if(t.run.work.visits!=7||t.events.size()!=9)throw std::runtime_error("tiny work");

}
```
