\image(figures/gnome_original.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The original 27-visit pointer walk now comes from the same core execution that sorts the values. Its ten backward steps remove ten inversions. Three boundary visits explain why 27 visits contain only 24 key comparisons.)
\alttext(A blue pointer path rises and retreats over all twenty-seven visits of the original seven-value example. The complete printed table distinguishes visits that compare keys, visits that swap, and visits at the boundary.)

The scalar API still returns an owned sorted copy. It sorts that owned buffer in
place using constant auxiliary state, but passing an lvalue copies n values.
`gnome_sort_run()` additionally creates and returns n original-position labels;
that output and its initialization cost O(n). The trace adds O(H) fixed-size
records, rather than retaining a complete n-value snapshot for each visit.

> Equal values retain their identities

Sorting integers alone cannot visibly distinguish two equal keys. The diagnostic
API carries original indices alongside the actual swaps. For [2,1,2,1], the two
ones must retain identities 1 then 3, while the twos retain 0 then 2. The diagram
connects each input identity to its actual final slot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gnome_stability.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gnome_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const std::vector<int> input{2,1,2,1};const auto r=dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_run(input);
 std::print("| sorted slot | value | original index |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<r.output.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",i,r.output[i],r.original_indices[i]);
 std::print("\nStable output {}; identities {}; swaps {}; visits {}.\n",r.output,r.original_indices,r.work.swaps,r.work.visits);
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(78,1000);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=1.7;box.height=1.1;box.font_size=22;
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<input.size();++i){
  box.fill=input[i]==1?dm::graphics::RGB{254,243,199}:dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254};
  d.node(std::format("in{}",i),{2.6*double(i),2.6},std::format("value {}\nid {}",input[i],i),box);
 }
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<r.output.size();++i){
  box.fill=r.output[i]==1?dm::graphics::RGB{254,243,199}:dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254};
  d.node(std::format("out{}",i),{2.6*double(i),0},std::format("value {}\nid {}",r.output[i],r.original_indices[i]),box);
 }
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<r.output.size();++i)d.edge(std::format("in{}",r.original_indices[i]),std::format("out{}",i));
 d.text({3.9,4},"Original keys and identities",24)
  .text({3.9,-1.2},"Equal-key identities keep their original order",22).save_svg("build/gnome_stability.svg");
 if(r.original_indices!=std::vector<std::size_t>{1,3,0,2})throw std::runtime_error("stable identities");

}
