\caption(The descending family has n² visits. Moving a single minimum to the far end is still linear, with 3n−2 visits. One adjacent inversion costs only two visits beyond ascending input; this makes the role of disorder precise.)
\alttext(Four count curves compare ascending, descending, one adjacent inversion and a last-position minimum for nine input lengths. Every actual count is compared with its independent inversion-based prediction in a printed table.)

> Visits and key comparisons are different quantities

Two four-value inputs can have the same inversion count but different boundary
counts. [4,1,2,3] and [3,2,1,4] each have three inversions and ten visits. Their
strict new prefix minima differ, producing two versus three boundary visits and
therefore eight versus seven key comparisons. An all-equal input has no swaps:
its four visits include one boundary step and three comparisons.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gnome_comparisons.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gnome_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const std::vector<std::vector<int>> inputs{{4,1,2,3},{3,2,1,4},{7,7,7,7}};
 const std::vector<std::string> names{"Front maximum","Reverse prefix","All equal"};
 std::vector<double> visits,comparisons;
 std::print("| input | swaps = strict inversions | visits | boundary visits | key comparisons |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<inputs.size();++i){
  const auto r=dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_run(inputs[i]);
  std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",names[i],r.work.swaps,r.work.visits,r.work.boundary_visits,r.work.key_comparisons);
  visits.push_back(double(r.work.visits));comparisons.push_back(double(r.work.key_comparisons));
 }
 auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(visits,names),b=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(comparisons,names);
 a.title("Every executed loop body").xlab("").ylab("Visits").y_limits(0,12);
 b.title("Boundary visits do not compare keys").xlab("").ylab("Key comparisons").y_limits(0,10);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,500).title("Equal inversion counts need not give equal comparison counts").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gnome_comparisons.svg");
 if(visits!=std::vector<double>{10,10,4}||comparisons!=std::vector<double>{8,7,3})throw std::runtime_error("comparison identities");

}
