\alttext(Two bar charts compare visits and key comparisons for a front maximum, a reversed three-value prefix and an all-equal input. The first two visit counts are ten, while comparison counts are eight and seven; all-equal gives four visits and three comparisons.)

> Complete histories and whole generated inputs have different units

`gnome_sort_trace()` captures fixed-size initial, step and stop records online.
A completed S-visit execution has S+2 records; there is no full-vector snapshot
per visit or numerical replay. Before each complete append, the optional quota
and container capacity are checked. Even the final metadata append can throw:
no partial history or ordinary result is returned. Zero turns off the optional
record quota; it does not suppress recording.

A quota counts complete records, not numeric entries, bytes or peak RAM. Inputs,
the root object, ordinary sorted values and identity output, constant working
state and allocator overhead are excluded. Input copying and identity allocation
can happen before a history limit is reached. The generator instead checks the
whole 4n integer entries across its four arrays before allocating them. Its entry
quota also excludes vector objects and allocator overhead. These controls have
different meanings even when their numeric limits happen to coincide.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gnome_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gnome_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 std::vector<int> input{2,1};const auto original=input;
 bool record_rejected=false,empty_rejected=false,values_rejected=false;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_trace(input,5);}catch(const std::length_error&){record_rejected=true;}
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_trace(input,6);
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_trace({},1);}catch(const std::length_error&){empty_rejected=true;}
 const auto empty=dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_trace({},2);
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::adjacent_sort_inputs(4,15);}catch(const std::length_error&){values_rejected=true;}
 const auto f=dm::algorithms::adjacent_sort_inputs(4,16);
 const auto total=f.ascending.size()+f.descending.size()+f.adjacent_inversion.size()+f.last_minimum.size();
 auto copy=t;copy.events[0].index_before=999;copy.run.output[0]=999;
 std::print("| resource | retained amount | rejected limit | rejected |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Two-value complete history | {} | 5 | {} |\n| Empty initial and stop metadata | {} | 1 | {} |\n| Whole four-array input family | {} | 15 | {} |\n",t.events.size(),record_rejected,empty.events.size(),empty_rejected,total,values_rejected);
 std::print("\nZero optional history quota retains {} records; zero optional family quota generates {} entries. Independent owned copy {}; caller input unchanged {}.\n",dm::algorithms::gnome_sort_trace(input,0).events.size(),4*dm::algorithms::adjacent_sort_inputs(4,0).ascending.size(),t.events[0].index_before!=copy.events[0].index_before&&t.run.output[0]!=copy.run.output[0],input==original);
 auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(t.events.size()),5.},{"Retained","Rejected cap"});
 a.title("Online history, including metadata").xlab("").ylab("Complete records").y_limits(0,8);
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(total),15.},{"Generated","Rejected cap"});
 p.title("Four arrays admitted together").xlab("").ylab("Integer entries").y_limits(0,20);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(p).size(1100,500).title("Online records and whole generated entries are separate resources").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gnome_controls.svg");
 if(!record_rejected||!empty_rejected||!values_rejected||input!=original)throw std::runtime_error("resource controls");

}
```
